WEBVTT

00:00:00.116 --> 00:00:04.522
Pinecone represents a managed-cloud approach to vector search.

00:00:04.522 --> 00:00:10.017
The application connects using an API key and an existing index.

00:00:10.017 --> 00:00:17.122
We insert vectors with IDs and metadata, then send a query vector and request the top results.

00:00:17.122 --> 00:00:23.262
The advantage of a managed service is that much of the infrastructure work is handled for you.

00:00:23.262 --> 00:00:30.512
The tradeoff is that you now depend on a cloud service, authentication, network access, vendor pricing,

00:00:30.512 --> 00:00:33.037
and vendor-specific APIs. [tts-break]

00:00:33.037 --> 00:00:40.217
The code pattern should still look familiar: create embeddings, upsert records, embed the query,

00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:46.892
and retrieve nearest matches. For students, the goal is not to memorize a cloud SDK.

00:00:46.892 --> 00:00:53.977
The goal is to recognize the same RAG storage pattern in a different environment.

00:00:53.977 --> 00:01:00.960
In a real project, the decision would include cost, latency, compliance, availability, and team experience.
